  "rules": [
    "When recent history shows a strong downtrend (e.g., Example 1) but the model forecasts a slow, steady uptick, apply a negative bias correction of -5% to -8% to account for mean reversion and volatility expansion.",
    "If sentiment history contains mixed signals (both positive and negative spikes) within the last 7 days, the model's linear projection is significantly biased upward; reduce the forecast by approximately 10-12% to capture high-frequency reversals.",
    "The model consistently underestimates immediate volatility spikes following a period of consolidation; when true outcomes deviate >5% from forecasts in the first 5 days, apply a dynamic correction factor that increases variance rather than shifting the mean.",
    "In volatile regimes (standard deviation of history > 3), the model's horizon-specific error grows linearly with time; reduce long-term (20-30 day) forecast targets by 15% to prevent over-smoothing of price action."
  ]
